    "result_text": "The test suite is green (the AcceptanceTest is the only test class in the repo, and it passes). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain email blocklist, rejecting owner requests with a `400` when the email's domain is one of `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, or `guerrillamail.com`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainException.java` \u2014 checked exception (extends `Exception`) so it surfaces as an escalation.\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"error\": \"...\"}`.\n- `rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerEmailDomain.java` \u2014 reads the bound `OwnerFieldsDto`, extracts the domain (email already trimmed/lower-cased by the prior `NormalizeOwnerEmail` step), and throws when blocklisted. Email stays optional (no-op when absent/blank).\n- `officefloor/escalation/...DisposableEmailDomainException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n\n**Wiring:** inserted a `validateEmailDomain` step immediately after `normalizeEmail` in both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (carrying the `govern: [ transaction ]` in the PUT pipeline to match its neighbors).\n\nPlacing the check right after normalization means the domain is compared in its canonical lower-cased form, and running it before the postcode/uniqueness/persistence steps ensures the blocklisted request is rejected without side effects.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (posting `x@mailinator.com`) and the full suite pass with 0 failures/errors.",
